request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands  (The request says "completed", but the codebase stores completion in Todo.done, which is what the complete command sets. I'm reading "completed" as `done` instead of adding a new field. The plan adds a clear variant to Command in types, plus a pure clear function, parseArgs support and run support in commands.)
round 1: owners types=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 5 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 2: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 18/18 tests pass). Command now has a { kind: "clear" } variant. commands exports clear(todos), which drops todos with done === true (the field the request calls "completed"). It keeps order and doesn't mutate the input. parseArgs handles "clear". The acceptance test checks all of this.)

